\description{
Read any file mzLib recognises into a table of that format's own record fields, naming every field that could not become a column.

The many-files form of \code{\link{readers_read_records}}. Every file must have the same mzLib record type,
because one table has one column set: a list mixing record types is refused, naming the groups,
before any file is parsed. Split such a list by \code{file_type} from \code{\link{readers_identify_many}}
first.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_read_batch}. \code{records} begins with \code{source_index} (1-based, into \code{paths}) and
  \code{source_path}, then the format's own columns. \code{files} has one row per input: \code{record_type},
  \code{record_count} in records, \code{skipped_count} in items for mzIdentML, \code{caveats},
  \code{excluded_fields}, \code{failed_fields} and the error columns. \code{file_count}, \code{read_count} and
  \code{failed_count} count files; \code{record_count} and \code{returned_count} count records; \code{row_count}
  counts the rows of \code{records}.

}
